 "干る": "جَافّ, ناشف (Free from or lacking moisture.) / جَفَّ, جَفّ (To exhaust; to cause to run dry.)  [to dry (up)] / [to ebb ; to recede]",
 "干乾し": "جُوع شَدِيد (A condition of severe suffering due to a lack of nutrition.)  [starvation]",
 "干天": "جَفَاف (A period of unusually low rainfall, longer and more severe than a dry spell.)  [drought]\nمثال: 農夫たちは干天のため冬作の穀物は不作だろうとなげいた。\n→ The farmers complained that because of the dry weather there would be a poor harvest of winter grain.",
 "干戈": "سِلَاح, أَسْلِحَة (An instrument of attack or defense in combat or hunting, e.g. most guns, missile)  [weapon] / صِرَاع (The act or process of contending; violence or conflict.)  [fighting]",
 "干渉": "تَدَاخُل (The act of interfering with something, or something that interferes.) / تَدَاخُل (An effect caused by the superposition of two systems of waves.)  [interference]\nمثال: 僕のことに干渉しないでくれ。\n→ Don't interfere in my affairs.",
 "干渉的": "مُلْتَحِم, مُتَرَابِط (Orderly, logical and consistent.)  [coherent] / متطفل (Characterized or marked by meddling; inclined or having a tendency to meddle or )  [meddlesome]",
 "干犯": "مِسَاس (A violation or breach, as of a law.)  [infringement]",
 "干肉": "قَدِيد (Lean meat cured and preserved by cutting into thin strips and air-drying in the )  [jerky]",
 "干草": "تِبْن, جَفِيف (Grass cut and dried for use as animal fodder.)  [hay]\nمثال: 干し草を納屋に蓄えた。\n→ We stored the hay in the barn.",
 "平": "[something broad and flat]\nمثال: 人は昔地球は平だと思っていた。\n→ People once held that the world was flat. / شَائِع (Found in large numbers or in a large quantity; usual.) / شَائِع (Simple, ordinary or vulgar.)  [common] / خَاصّ, شَخْصِيّ (Belonging or pertaining to an individual person, group of people, or entity that) / خَاصّ (Not traded by the public.) / جُنْدِيّ (A soldier of the lowest rank in the army.)  [private]\nمثال: 他の役職なんて残ってないし。あとは平部員だけだよ。\n→ Well there aren't any other positions left. After that, all that is left is basic member.",
 "平々": "مُسْتَوًى (A distance relative to a given reference elevation.) / مُسْتَوًى (Degree or amount.) / مَرْحَلَة (One of several discrete segments of a game, generally increasing in difficulty a)  [level]",
 "平々凡々": "مُتَوَسِّط (Not excellent or outstanding, usually disappointingly so.)  [mediocre]\nمثال: 彼ほど平々凡々たる主人公は珍しい。\n→ A protagonist as plain and ordinary as him is rare indeed.",
 "平か": "مُسْتَوًى (A distance relative to a given reference elevation.) / مُسْتَوًى (Degree or amount.) / مَرْحَلَة (One of several discrete segments of a game, generally increasing in difficulty a)  [level]",
 "平し": "مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Any measure of central tendency, especially any mean, the median, or the mode.) / مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Constituting or relating to the average.)  [average]\nمثال: 彼らはブルドーザーで道ならしをしている。\n→ They are now leveling the road with a bulldozer.",
 "平たい": "مُسَطَّح (having no variations in altitude)  [flat]\nمثال: 古代人たちは地球は平たいと信じていた。\n→ The ancients believed the earth was flat. / بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain (language, words, etc.)]\nusu. as 平たく言えば, 平たく言うと, etc.",
 "平ちゃら": "غَيْر مُكْتَرِث, لَامُبَالٍ (Indifferent; unconcerned; behaving as if detached.)  [nonchalant]\nمثال: 先生に怒られたってへっちゃらだい。\n→ I couldn't care less if the teacher is mad at me. / سَهْل (Requiring little skill or effort.)  [easy]",
 "平ったい": "مُسَطَّح (having no variations in altitude)  [flat] / بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain (language, words, etc.)]",
 "平に": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please (e.g. forgive me)]\nusu. followed by a request\nمثال: どうかひらにご容赦ください。\n→ Please accept my humble apologies.",
 "平べったい": "مُسَطَّح (having no variations in altitude)  [flat]",
 "平ら": "مُسَطَّح (having no variations in altitude)  [flat]\nمثال: あの山の頂上は平らだ。\n→ The top of that mountain is flat. / هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm] / اِسْتَرْخَى (To become loose.)  [relaxed (sitting posture)]\nusu. as お平らに / هَضْبَة (A largely level expanse of land at a high elevation; tableland.)  [plateau]\nafter a place name, usu. だいら",
 "平らか": "مُسْتَوًى (A distance relative to a given reference elevation.) / مُسْتَوًى (Degree or amount.) / مَرْحَلَة (One of several discrete segments of a game, generally increasing in difficulty a)  [level]",
 "平らげる": "[to eat up (completely)]\nمثال: 彼はごちそうをすっかり平らげた。\n→ He ate every bit of his dinner. / اِسْتَعْبَدَ, قَهَرَ (To forcibly impose obedience, servitude, or submission upon (a country, a people)  [to subjugate] / [to make flat ; to level out]",
 "平仄": "مِقْيَاس (measuring instrument) / وَزْن (rhythm of poetry) / بَحْر (rhythm of poetry)  [meter (in Chinese poetry)]\nمثال: 脚韻と平仄が漢詩の基本的ルールとなっています。\n→ Rhyme and meter form the essential rules of Chinese poetry.",
 "平仮名": "هِيرَاغَانَا (Japanese syllabary)  [hiragana]",
 "平俗": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary] / [informal and easy to understand (of writing, etc.)]",
 "平凡": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]\nمثال: その模様の色は実に平凡なものである。\n→ The colors of the pattern are very ordinary.",
 "平削り": "مِسْحَاج, مِنْجَرَة (A tool for smoothing wood by removing thin layers from the surface.) / سَحَجَ (To smooth (wood) with a plane.) / طَائِرَة, طَيَّارَة (An airplane; an aeroplane.) / دُلْب, صِنَار (A deciduous tree of the genus Platanus.)  [planing (of a surface)]",
 "平原": "بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain]\nمثال: 初秋の頃のほど、その平原が美しく見えるときはない。\n→ At no time does the plain look so perfect as in early autumn.",
 "平台型貨車": "مَصْطَبَة (A railroad freight car without sides and roof.)  [flatcar]",
 "平和": "سَلَام, هُدُوء (A state of tranquility, quiet, and harmony. For instance, a state free from civi) / سَلَام (Harmony in personal relations.)  [peace]\nمثال: ハトは平和のシンボルである。\n→ The dove is a symbol of peace.",
 "平和主義": "سَلَامِيَّة, سِلْمِيَّة (The additional challenge of winning a game without harming any enemy characters.)  [pacifism]",
 "平和主義者": "مُسَالِم (one who loves, supports, or favours peace) / مُسَالِمَة (one who loves, supports, or favours peace)  [pacifist]",
 "平和共存": "تَعَايُش سِلْمِيّ (A situation where nation-states do not interfere with the domestic affairs of ot)  [peaceful coexistence]",
 "平和思想": "سَلَامِيَّة, سِلْمِيَّة (The additional challenge of winning a game without harming any enemy characters.)  [pacifism]",
 "平和条約": "مُعَاهَدَة سَلَام (An agreement to end fighting or conflict.)  [peace treaty]\nمثال: １９７８年に日本と中国との間に平和条約が結ばれた。\n→ In 1978 a peace treaty was concluded between Japan and China.",
 "平和的": "سِلْمِيّ (Not at war; not disturbed by strife or turmoil.) / مُسَالِم (Inclined to peace.)  [peaceful]\nمثال: マーティン・ルーサー・キング牧師の支持者の中には、平和的に抗議するという彼の信念に疑いの念を持つ物も現れ始めた。\n→ Some of Martin Luther King's supporters began to question his belief in peaceful protests.",
 "平和維持": "حِفْظ سَلَام (The act of preserving peace, specifically between hostile groups or states, espe)  [peacekeeping]",
 "平和裏": "سِلْمِيّ (Not at war; not disturbed by strife or turmoil.) / مُسَالِم (Inclined to peace.)  [peaceful]\nusu. 平和裏に",
 "平和論者": "مُسَالِم (one who loves, supports, or favours peace) / مُسَالِمَة (one who loves, supports, or favours peace)  [pacifist]",
 "平土間": "حُفْرَة (A hole in the ground.)  [pit]",
 "平地": "بَسِيط (Simple, unaltered.) / سَهْل (An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy)  [plain]\nمثال: 飛行機から見ると、小さな丘陵は平地のように見える。\n→ Small hills look flat from an airplane.",
 "平均": "مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Any measure of central tendency, especially any mean, the median, or the mode.) / مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Constituting or relating to the average.)  [average]\nمثال: 今年の冬は気温が平均以上だ。\n→ The temperature is above average this winter. / رَصِيد (A list accounting for the debits on one side, and for the credits on the other.)  [balance]",
 "平均余命": "مَأْمُول اَلْحَيَاة, مُتَوَسِّط العُمْر المُتَوَقَّع (The amount of time one is expected to live.)  [life expectancy]",
 "平均値": "عَنَى, عَنَى (To convey (a meaning).) / لَئِيم, خَسِيس (Intending to cause harm, successfully or otherwise; bearing ill will towards ano) / مُتَوَسِّط (the statistical value)  [mean]\nمثال: 周波数の平均値は振幅の増大にしたがって減じる。\n→ The mean value of the frequency decreases with increasing amplitude.",
 "平均化": "مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Any measure of central tendency, especially any mean, the median, or the mode.) / مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Constituting or relating to the average.)  [averaging]",
 "平均寿命": "مَأْمُول اَلْحَيَاة, مُتَوَسِّط العُمْر المُتَوَقَّع (The amount of time one is expected to live.)  [life expectancy (at birth)]\nمثال: 最近の研究によれば、日本人の平均寿命はまだ伸びているそうだ。\n→ According to a recent study, the average life span of the Japanese is still increasing. / [mean lifetime]",
 "平均的": "مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Any measure of central tendency, especially any mean, the median, or the mode.) / مُتَوَسِّط, مُعَدَّل (Constituting or relating to the average.)  [average]\nمثال: 彼は平均的な背丈だ。\n→ He was a man of average height.",
 "平坦": "مُسَطَّح, مُنبَسِط (Flat and level.) / أَمْلَس, سَوِيّ (Without great variation.) / زَوْجِيّ (Of an integer, divisible by two.) / حَتَّى (In reality (used to imply an extreme example in the case mentioned).)  [even] / هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm]\nمثال: 平和への道は決して平坦ではない。\n→ The road to peace is never smooth.",
