 "平然": "هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm]\nمثال: その政治家は平然と賄賂を受け取り、全ての契約の５％が濡れ手に粟で彼の懐に入った。\n→ The politician had sticky fingers, and 5% of every contract ended in his pocket.",
 "平爪": "ظُفْر, ضفر (The horny plate or appendage at the ends of the digits of various animals, inclu) / مِسْمَار, مسمار (A spike-shaped metal fastener used for joining wood or similar materials. The na)  [nail (e.g. fingernail, toenail)]",
 "平生": "عَادِيّ (Most commonly occurring; typical.)  [usual]",
 "平癒": "شِفَاء, تَعَافِي (A return to normal health.)  [recovery]",
 "平穏": "هَادِئ (Peaceful, quiet, especially free from anger and anxiety.) / طَمْأَنَ (To make calm.)  [calm]\nمثال: その市は一週間後に平穏に復した。\n→ The city was restored to tranquility after a week.",
 "平穏無事": "سِلْمِيّ (Not at war; not disturbed by strife or turmoil.) / مُسَالِم (Inclined to peace.)  [peaceful]\nمثال: だれしも、楽しい青春を平穏無事な時期として想い起こす。\n→ Everyone remembers the happy days of his youth as his halcyon days.",
 "平等": "مُسَاوَاة (The fact of being equal.) / تَسَاوٍ (The fact of being equal, of having the same value.) / مُسَاوَاة (The equal treatment of people irrespective of social or cultural differences.)  [equality]\nمثال: すべての人間が平等に創られているわけではない。\n→ Not all men are created equal.",
