 "幾": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]\nbefore a counter or noun + か\nمثال: 白いガラスに、幾色かの色ガラスが入り、かわいらしい印象に仕上がりました。\n→ To the white glass, I added glass of various colours, producing a pretty feel. / كَثِير (before a countable noun: A large, indefinite number of.) / كَثِير, متعدد (A large, indefinite number of people or things.)  [many]\nbefore a counter or noun (+も)\nمثال: いく層もの卸業者の存在が特色である日本の流通機構は、複雑でコストもかかる。\n→ The Japanese distribution system, characterized by layers of wholesale, is complex and costly. / كَم / كَمْ (what number)  [how many] / جِدًّا (To a great extent or degree.)  [very]\nbefore an adjective",
 "幾たび": "كَثِيرًا, غَالِبًا (Frequently; many times on different occasions.)  [(how) often]\nمثال: 今日の幸せが幾度も巡ってきますように。\n→ Many happy returns of the day! Happy birthday!",
 "幾つ": "كَم / كَمْ (what number)  [how many]\nمثال: いいえ、おもちゃがいくつあるかじゃなくて、鍵がいくつあるかなのよ。\n→ No, not how many toys, how many keys? / [how old]\nمثال: あなたのお父さんはおいくつですか。\n→ How old is your father?",
 "幾つか": "قَلِيل (An indefinite, but usually small, number of.) / قَلِيل (Not many; a small (in comparison with another number stated or implied) but some) / قَلِيل (Few people, few things.)  [(a) few]\nمثال: いくつかの点で私は彼女が気に入らない。\n→ I don't like her in some ways.",
 "幾つも": "كَثِير (before a countable noun: A large, indefinite number of.) / كَثِير, متعدد (A large, indefinite number of people or things.)  [many]\nمثال: この市にはいくつもの映画館がある。\n→ There are many movie theaters in this city. / [hardly]\nin neg. sentence",
 "幾ばく": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much]\nمثال: 彼は余命いくばくもない。\n→ His days are drawing to their close.",
 "幾ばくか": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]",
 "幾ほど": "كَم / كَمْ (what number)  [how many]",
 "幾ら": "كَمْ (What amount or quantity of (something stated or implied).)  [how much]\nمثال: 入場料はいくらですか。\n→ How much is the entrance fee? / [something over ; and something]\nafter a rounded number, esp. a sum of money / بِأَيَّةِ طَرِيقَة, عَلَى كُلِّ حَال (In any way that one likes or chooses; in a haphazard or spontaneous way.)  [however (much)]\nas いくら...〜ても, いくら...〜でも, etc.\nمثال: 私がいくら言っても、聞こうとしないのよ。\n→ You never listen, no matter how many times I tell you.",
 "幾らか": "بَعْضٌ (A certain number (multiple but not all).) / بَعْض (An indefinite quantity.) / بَعْض (An indefinite amount; a part. Used mostly with abstract and nonliving objects.) / بَعْضٌ (A nonzero, unspecified proportion of (a bounded set of countable things): at lea)  [some]\nمثال: 彼女は非常の場合に備えていくらか貯金した。\n→ She put by some money for a rainy day. / [somewhat ; to some extent]\nمثال: クリスマスが近づくにつれて景気はいくらか回復した。\n→ With the approach of Christmas, business improved somewhat.",
 "幾らでも": "[as many as one likes ; as much as one likes]\nمثال: 好きな花をいくらでも選びなさい。\n→ Choose any flowers you like. / كَثِير (A more-than-adequate amount; plenitude; a great deal.)  [plenty]\nمثال: 彼はいくらでもお金を出せる。\n→ He can come up with any amount of money. / تَقْرِيبًا, عَلَى وَشْك (Very close to, but not quite.)  [almost (none)]\nas いくらでもない / [no matter how much ; no matter how big or small]",
 "幾らにもならない": "بَخْس (meager; worthless; pitiful; trifling)  [paltry]",
 "幾らも": "كَثِير (A large amount.) / كَثِيرًا (Very much; a great deal; to a large extent.) / كَثِيرًا (Often; frequently.)  [a lot] / كَثِير (A large amount of.) / كَثِيرًا (to a great extent)  [(not) much]\nwith neg. verb\nمثال: 金はいくらも持ってない。\n→ I have little money.",
 "幾世": "جِيل, نَسْل (A single step or stage in the succession of natural descent; a rank or degree in) / جِيل (The average amount of time needed for children to grow up and have children of t)  [generations]\nمثال: この儀式は幾世代にもわたって伝わってきた。\n→ This ceremony has been handed down from generation to generation.",
