 "弌": "وَاحِد, وَاحِدَة (The number represented by the Arabic numeral 1; the numerical value equal to tha) / اَلْمَرْء (Any person (applying to people in general).)  [one]\n壱, 弌 and 壹 are used in legal documents\nمثال: それは壱万円と計算されている。\n→ It is computed at 10,000 yen. / أَفْضَل (superlative form of good: most good.)  [best]\nمثال: これは東京一のインドレストランです。\n→ This is the best Indian restaurant anywhere in Tokyo. / أَوَّل, أُولَى (Coming right after the zeroth in things that use zero-based numbering.) / أَوَّلاً (Before anything else; firstly.) / أَوَّل (The person or thing in the first position.)  [first]\nمثال: 津山一高い山は滝山だと思っていました。\n→ I thought the highest mountain in Tsuyama was Takiyama. / بِدَايَة (The act of doing that which begins anything; commencement of an action, state, o) / بِدَايَة (That which begins or originates something; the source or first cause.) / بِدَايَة (The initial portion of some extended thing.)  [beginning]",
