 "引き抜き": "تَعْبِئَة (The process or art of finding candidates for a post in an organization, or recru)  [recruitment]\nمثال: 社長は新しいセールスマネージャーを入れるため、引き抜き専門の人物を雇った。\n→ The company president has hired a headhunter to find us a new sales manager. / [quick costume change (taking off outer costume)] / رَسْم (A picture, likeness, diagram or representation, usually drawn on paper.) / رَسْم (The act of producing such a picture.)  [drawing (wire, pipes, metal plate)] / [extraction ; pulling out]",
 "引き抜く": "مُقْتَطَف (A portion of a book, document, recording etc. incorporated distinctly in another) / خلاصة (A decoction, solution, or infusion made by drawing out from any substance that w)  [to extract]\nمثال: 歯科医は彼女の虫歯を引き抜いた。\n→ The dentist pulled out her bad tooth. / [to headhunt ; to lure away]\nمثال: 彼はライバル会社に引き抜かれました。\n→ He was poached by a rival company.",
 "引き揚げ": "[pulling up ; drawing up] / رَفَعَ (to cause to rise)  [raising]\nمثال: 関税引き上げの提案国はお互いに反目しています。\n→ Proponents of increased import duties are at odds with each other. / إخْلَاء, تَخْلِيَة (The act of evacuating; leaving a place in an orderly fashion, especially for saf) / إخْلَاء (Withdrawal of troops or civils from a town, country, fortress, etc.) / تَفْرِيغ, تَخْلِيَة (The act of emptying, clearing of the contents, or discharging, including creatin)  [evacuation]",
 "引き揚げる": "رَفَعَ (To elevate to a higher position.)  [to lift up]\nمثال: 引き上げてくれ。\n→ Give me a hoist. / زَاد (To make (a quantity, etc.) larger.) / زِيَادَة (An amount by which a quantity is increased.) / اِرْتِفَاع, اِزْدِيَاد (For a quantity, the act or process of becoming larger.)  [to increase]\nمثال: 政府は近々、消費税を引き上げるつもりなのかしら。\n→ Will the government raise the consumption tax soon? / سَحَبَ (To extract (money) from a bank account or other financial deposit.) / تَرَاجَعَ (Chiefly followed by from: to leave a place, someone's presence, etc., to go to a)  [to withdraw]\nمثال: 彼は夕食後自室に引き上げた。\n→ He retired to his own room after supper. / رَقَّى (To raise (someone) to a more important, responsible, or remunerative job or rank) / رَوَّجَ (To advocate or urge on behalf of (something or someone); to attempt to populariz)  [to promote (someone to a higher position)]",
 "引き換え": "تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [exchange]\nمثال: 彼はお金と引換に切符を受け取った。\n→ He received a ticket in return for the money.",
 "引き換えて": "عَلَى الْعَكْس, بِالْعَكْس (Opposite of what had earlier been expected or assumed; to the contrary.)  [on the contrary]",
 "引き換える": "تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [to exchange (things)] / [to be in contrast (to) ; to contrast (with)]\nusu. as 〜に引き換え(て)",
 "引き換え券": "قَسِيمَة (A section of a ticket, showing the holder to be entitled to some specified accom) / قَسِيمَة (A voucher issued by a manufacturer or retailer which offers a discount on a part) / كُوبُون, كُوبُون (A certificate of interest due, printed at the bottom of transferable bonds (stat)  [coupon]\nمثال: 引き換え券を見せて下さい。\n→ May I see your claim tags?",
 "引き換え証": "إِيصَال (A written acknowledgment that a specified article or sum of money has been recei)  [receipt]\nمثال: 搭乗券と荷物の引き換え証です。\n→ Here are your boarding pass and your baggage claim.",
 "引き摺る": "جَرَّ (To pull along a surface or through a medium, sometimes with difficulty.)  [to drag]\nمثال: 私は重い荷物を空港まで引きずって行った。\n→ I dragged the heavy baggage to the airport. / جَرَّ (To pull along a surface or through a medium, sometimes with difficulty.)  [to drag (along)]\nمثال: 彼は彼女の腕を取り、引きずっていった。\n→ He seized her hand and dragged her away. / أَطَالَ (To extend in space or length.) / أَطَالَ (To lengthen in time; to extend the duration of.)  [to prolong] / نَفُوذ, تَأْثِير (The power to affect, control or manipulate something or someone; the ability to ) / تَأْثِير (An action exerted by a person or thing with such power on another to cause chang) / أَثَّرَ (To have an effect on by using gentle or subtle action; to exert an influence upo)  [to influence]\nusu. in the passive",
 "引き攣り": "نَدْبَة, نَدْب (A permanent mark on the skin, sometimes caused by the healing of a wound.)  [scar] / تَشَنُّج (A sudden, involuntary contraction of a muscle, a group of muscles, or a hollow o)  [spasm]",
 "引き攣る": "زِيَار (A stick with a hole in one end through which passes a loop, which can be drawn t)  [to twitch]\nمثال: 顔がひきつります。\n→ My face twitches. / جَمَدَ (To become stiff.)  [to stiffen (of a face, expression)]\nمثال: ジョンの顔は引きつっていた。\n→ John's face was drawn. / قَلَّصَ (To cause to become smaller.) / تَقَلَّصَ, أَحْجَمَ (To become smaller; to contract.)  [to shrink (of skin, due to a scar)]",
 "引き数": "جِدَال, مُجَادَلَة (A verbal dispute; a quarrel.) / وَسِيط (A value, or a reference to a value, passed to a function.)  [argument (of a function)]",
 "引き明け": "فَجْر (To begin to brighten with daylight.) / فَجْر, فَلَق (The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.) / شُرُوق (The rising of the sun.) / شُرُوق, مَشْرِق (The time when the sun rises.) / فَجْر (The earliest phase of something.)  [dawn]",
 "引き替え": "تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [exchange]\nمثال: 彼はお金と引換に切符を受け取った。\n→ He received a ticket in return for the money.",
