 "引き移る": "حَرُكَ, تَحَرَّكَ (To change place or posture; to go, in any manner, from one place or position to ) / اِنْتَقَلَ, تَحَلْحَلَ (To change residence, for example from one house, town, or state, to another; to )  [to move]",
 "引き立つ": "[to cheer up ; to liven up] / حَسَّنَ (To make (something) better; to increase the value or productivity (of something)) / تَحَسَّنَ (To become better.)  [to improve (in appearance)]\nمثال: 赤いベルトが彼女の黒いドレスをひきたたせている。\n→ The red belt makes her black dress look even better.",
 "引き立て": "مَعْرُوف (A kind or helpful deed; an instance of voluntarily assisting (someone).) / أَنْعَمَ (To look upon fondly; to prefer.)  [favor] / دَعَمَ, دَعَّمَ (To help keep from falling.) / أَيَّدَ, دَعَمَ (To back or favor a cause, party, etc., mentally or with concrete aid) / تَأْيِيد, دَعْم (Financial or other help.)  [support]",
 "引き立てる": "[to set off to advantage ; to bring into prominence] / دَعَمَ, دَعَّمَ (To help keep from falling.) / أَيَّدَ, دَعَمَ (To back or favor a cause, party, etc., mentally or with concrete aid) / تَأْيِيد, دَعْم (Financial or other help.)  [to support] / [to rouse (spirits)] / [to march (a prisoner) off ; to haul someone off]",
