 "引き離す": "فَصَلَ (To disunite from a group or mass; to disconnect.) / مُنْفَصِل (Apart from (the rest); not connected to or attached to (anything else).)  [to separate]\nمثال: 警官は取っ組み合いをしている二人の男を引き離した。\n→ The policeman separated the two men who were fighting. / [to have a lead over ; to pull ahead of]\nمثال: 私どもは完全に他社を引き離していますよ。\n→ We have completely outstripped the other companies.",
 "引く": "جَرَّ, سَحَبَ (To apply a force to (an object) so that it comes toward the person or thing appl)  [to pull]\nمثال: カーテンがゆっくり引かれた。\n→ The curtains were drawn slowly. / دَلَجَ, غَرَفَ (Senses relating to attracting.) / رَسَمَ (Senses relating to attracting.) / قُرْعَة (The act of drawing:)  [to draw (attention, sympathy, etc.)]\nalso written as 惹く / [to draw back (e.g. one's hand) ; to draw in (one's chin, stomach, etc.)]\nمثال: あんな本みたらフツーの女は引くもんな！\n→ Obviously a normal woman would lose interest if she saw a book like that! / دَلَجَ, غَرَفَ (Senses relating to attracting.) / رَسَمَ (Senses relating to attracting.) / قُرْعَة (The act of drawing:)  [to draw (a card, mahjong tile, etc.)]\nمثال: あなたの引いたカードは赤のマークですね。\n→ The card you drew was a red, wasn't it?",
