 "弾ずる": "لَعِبَ, لعب (To act in a manner such that one has fun; to engage in activities expressly for ) / عَزَفَ, عَزَفَ (To produce sound (especially music), moving pictures, or theatrical performance.) / دَوْر (A short sequence of action within a game.) / مَسْرَحِيَّة (A literary composition, intended to be represented by actors impersonating the c) / مَسْرَح, مَسْرَحِيَّة (A theatrical performance featuring actors.)  [to play (a stringed instrument)]",
 "弾み": "عَيْن, يَنْبُوع (Something which springs, springs forth, springs up, or springs back, particularl) / يَاي, زُنْبُرُك (Something which springs, springs forth, springs up, or springs back, particularl)  [spring] / زَخَم حَرَكَة (Of a body in motion: the tendency of a body to maintain its inertial motion; the) / زَخَم (The impetus, either of a body in motion, or of an idea or course of events; a mo)  [momentum]\nمثال: ドル安は輸出にはずみをつけています。\n→ The cheap dollar is charging up exports. / عَزْم (Ellipsis of moment of force.) / لَحْظَة, دَقِيقَة (A definite period of time, specifically one-tenth of a point, or one-fortieth or)  [moment]\nمثال: どういうはずみでここに来たのか自分でもわからない。\n→ I don't know what motivated me to come here.",
