 "必然": "حَتْمِيّ (Impossible to avoid or prevent.)  [inevitable] / ضَرُورَة, حَاجَة (The quality or state of being necessary, unavoidable, or absolutely requisite.)  [necessity]",
 "必然性": "ضَرُورَة, حَاجَة (The quality or state of being necessary, unavoidable, or absolutely requisite.)  [necessity]",
 "必然的": "حَتْمِيّ (Impossible to avoid or prevent.)  [inevitable]\nمثال: それは必然的に延期しなければならない。\n→ It must, of necessity, be postponed.",
 "必用": "ضَرُورِيّ, لَازِم (Required, essential, whether logically inescapable or needed in order to achieve)  [necessary]\n必用 can imply has to be used rather than is just needed\nمثال: 私達が生きていくためには衣食住が必要です。\n→ We need food, clothes and a home in order to live. / ضَرُورَة, حَاجَة (The quality or state of being necessary, unavoidable, or absolutely requisite.)  [necessity]\nمثال: 歯医者に行く必要はないですよ。\n→ You don't need to go to the dentist's.",
