 "忻然": "سَعِيد, مُفْرِح (Feeling or causing joy.)  [joyful]",
 "忽": "[one hundred-thousandth] / مُبَاغِت, مُفَاجِئ (Occurring quickly with little or no warning or expectation; instantly.)  [sudden]\nusu. 忽として",
 "忽せ": "غَيْر مُبَالِي (Not giving sufficient attention or thought, especially concerning the avoidance )  [careless]\nusu. adverbially as ～に / اِسْتَرْخَى (To become loose.)  [relaxed]",
 "忽せにする": "أَهْمَلَ (To omit to notice; to forbear to treat with attention or respect; to slight.) / إِهْمَال (The act of neglecting.)  [to neglect]",
 "忽ち": "فَوْرًا, حَالًا (In an immediate manner; instantly or without delay.)  [immediately]\nمثال: 切符はたちまち売り切れた。\n→ The tickets were sold out in a moment. / فَجْأَةً (Happening quickly and with little or no warning; in a sudden manner.)  [suddenly]",
 "忽地": "فَجْأَةً (Happening quickly and with little or no warning; in a sudden manner.)  [suddenly]",
 "忽焉": "مُبَاغِت, مُفَاجِئ (Occurring quickly with little or no warning or expectation; instantly.)  [sudden]",
 "忽然": "مُبَاغِت, مُفَاجِئ (Occurring quickly with little or no warning or expectation; instantly.)  [sudden]",
 "忿怒": "غَضَب (A strong and unpleasant feeling of displeasure, hostility, or antagonism, usuall) / أَغْضَبَ (To cause such a feeling of antagonism in.) / غَضِبَ (To become angry.)  [anger]",
 "怏々": "لَعُوق (Not happy; sad.)  [unhappy]",
 "怏怏": "لَعُوق (Not happy; sad.)  [unhappy]",
 "怒らす": "غَضَب (A strong and unpleasant feeling of displeasure, hostility, or antagonism, usuall) / أَغْضَبَ (To cause such a feeling of antagonism in.) / غَضِبَ (To become angry.)  [to anger]\nمثال: その猫を怒らすとひっかくよ。\n→ The cat will scratch you if you provoke it. / مُرَبَّع (A polygon with four straight sides of equal length and four right angles; an equ) / مُرَبَّع (Shaped like a square (the polygon).) / مُرَبَّع (Used in the names of units of area formed by multiplying a unit of length by its)  [to square (one's shoulders)]",
 "怒らせる": "غَضَب (A strong and unpleasant feeling of displeasure, hostility, or antagonism, usuall) / أَغْضَبَ (To cause such a feeling of antagonism in.) / غَضِبَ (To become angry.)  [to anger]\nمثال: 彼の無作法は仲間を怒らせた。\n→ His gross manners offended his companions. / مُرَبَّع (A polygon with four straight sides of equal length and four right angles; an equ) / مُرَبَّع (Shaped like a square (the polygon).) / مُرَبَّع (Used in the names of units of area formed by multiplying a unit of length by its)  [to square (one's shoulders)]\nمثال: 彼は肩を怒らせて歩いていた。\n→ He was walking with his shoulders squared.",
 "怒り": "غَضَب (A strong and unpleasant feeling of displeasure, hostility, or antagonism, usuall) / أَغْضَبَ (To cause such a feeling of antagonism in.) / غَضِبَ (To become angry.)  [anger]\nمثال: 私の誤りは彼の怒りを招いた。\n→ My mistake incurred his anger.",
 "怒りだす": "اِنْدَلَعَ (To burst out suddenly, as in anger.)  [to flare up]\nمثال: そうやってしつこく彼女を困らせると、彼女も怒り出すぞ。\n→ If you persist in bothering her like that, she'll lose her temper.",
 "怒りを買う": "أَهَانَ (To hurt the feelings of; to displease; to make angry; to insult.)  [to offend]",
 "怒り出す": "اِنْدَلَعَ (To burst out suddenly, as in anger.)  [to flare up]\nمثال: そうやってしつこく彼女を困らせると、彼女も怒り出すぞ。\n→ If you persist in bothering her like that, she'll lose her temper.",
 "怒り心頭": "حَنَق (Violent uncontrolled anger.) / غَضِبَ, اِنْدَلَعَ (To act or speak in heightened anger.)  [rage]",
 "怒り狂う": "حَنَق (Violent uncontrolled anger.) / غَضِبَ, اِنْدَلَعَ (To act or speak in heightened anger.)  [to rage]\nمثال: 彼は怒り狂っていた。\n→ He was beside himself with rage.",
 "怒る": "[to get angry ; to get mad]\nمثال: その子は留守番をしなければならないと言って怒っていた。\n→ The boy was cross at having to stay at home. / اِمْرَأَة سَلِيطَة (A person who habitually scolds, in particular a troublesome and angry woman.) / وَبَّخَ (To rebuke angrily.)  [to scold]\nusu. in the passive\nمثال: それをそのままにしておきなさい。そうしないと怒られますよ。\n→ Leave it as it is, or you will be scolded.",
 "怒気": "غَضَب (A strong and unpleasant feeling of displeasure, hostility, or antagonism, usuall) / أَغْضَبَ (To cause such a feeling of antagonism in.) / غَضِبَ (To become angry.)  [anger]\nمثال: 彼は怒気を顔に表した。\n→ He looked black with anger.",
 "怒涛": "[surging waves ; raging billows] / مُضْطَرِب, صَاخِب (Characterized by loud, confused noise.)  [tumultuous]",
 "怒濤": "[surging waves ; raging billows] / مُضْطَرِب, صَاخِب (Characterized by loud, confused noise.)  [tumultuous]",
 "怒鳴り出す": "اِنْدَلَعَ (To begin suddenly; to emerge in a certain condition.)  [to break out]\nمثال: 私が父にもっとお金をくれと言ったら父はすごくかっとなって私に向かって怒鳴りだした。\n→ When I asked Dad for more money, he really blew up and started to yell at me.",
 "怒鳴り散らす": "صَاحَ (To shout; holler; make a loud sound with the voice, especially to express intens)  [to yell]\nمثال: 私をどなり散らす人は気にならないわ。\n→ The ones who shout at me don't bother me.",
 "怒鳴る": "صَيح, صِيَاح (A loud burst of voice or voices; a violent and sudden outcry, especially that of) / صَرَخَ, صَاحَ (To utter a sudden and loud cry, as in joy, triumph, exultation or anger, or to a)  [to shout (in anger)]\nمثال: 泣いている子を怒鳴るな。火に油だから。\n→ Don't shout at the crying child. It only adds fuel to the fire.",
 "怖": "مُجَفِّل, مُخِيف (Causing fear; or capable of causing fear; scary.)  [frightening]\nمثال: 幼馴染ってこわ・・・。\n→ 'Childhood friends' are scary.",
 "怖い": "مُجَفِّل (Causing fear or anxiety)  [scary]\nمثال: 彼は君がヘビが恐いのかしらと思っている。\n→ He wonders if you are afraid of snakes.",
 "怖いもの知らず": "مُتَهَوِّر (Careless or heedless; headstrong or rash.)  [reckless]",
 "怖い物知らず": "مُتَهَوِّر (Careless or heedless; headstrong or rash.)  [reckless]",
 "怖がり": "جَبَان (A person who lacks courage.)  [coward]",
 "怖がる": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [to fear]\nمثال: 彼女はヘビをとてもこわがっている。\n→ She has a great fear of snakes.",
 "怖じけ": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [fear]",
 "怖じ気": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [fear]",
 "怖る": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [to fear]",
 "怖れる": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [to fear]\nمثال: 大人はしばしば変化を恐れる。\n→ Older people often fear change.",
 "怖気": "خَوْف, وَهَل (A strong, unpleasant emotion or feeling caused by actual or perceived danger or ) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To feel fear.) / خَافَ عَلَى, خَشِيَ عَلَى (To worry about, to feel concern for, to be afraid for [with for].) / خَافَ, خَشِيَ (To venerate; to feel awe towards.)  [fear]",
 "怜悧": "ذَكِيّ (Smart, intelligent, or witty; mentally quick or sharp.)  [clever]\nمثال: そういう相手の前では、私の見せ掛けだけの怜悧な技術は、見抜かれた時に負けていたと思う。\n→ I think that against somebody like that, my seemingly clever techniques would be seen through and then I would be defeated.",
 "怜悧狡猾": "مَاكِر (Sly; crafty; clever in surreptitious behaviour.)  [cunning]",
 "思い": "فِكْر, فِكْرَة (A representation created in the mind without the use of one's faculties of visio) / فِكْر, تَفْكِير (The operation by which mental activity arise or are manipulated; the process of )  [thought] / خَيَّال, تَخَيُّل (The image-making power of the mind; the act of mentally creating or reproducing ) / صُورَة ذِهْنِيَّة (A mental image formed by the action of the imagination as a faculty; something i)  [imagination] / رَغِبَ (To want; to wish for earnestly.) / رَغْبَة (Someone or something wished for.)  [desire] / حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [love]\ne.g. Ａ思いのＢ for 'B who loves A'",
 "思いあがり": "غَطْرَسَة (Excessive arrogance or pride, or presumption; originally (Greek mythology) towar)  [hubris]",
 "思いいれ": "[emotional attachment] / مَوْقِف, سُلُوك (A disposition or state of mind.)  [attitude (expressing emotion)]",
 "思いがけない": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: 彼は全く思いがけなく着いた。\n→ He arrived quite out of the blue.",
 "思いきり": "[to one's heart's content ; as much as one wants]\nمثال: 私は思いきり働きたい。\n→ I will work to the best of my ability. / عَزْم, عُزْم (A strong will; the state of being resolute.) / دِقَّة (The degree of fineness with which an image can be recorded or produced, often ex)  [resolution]",
 "思いこみ": "إِجْحَاف, تَحَامُل (An adverse judgment or opinion formed beforehand or without knowledge of the fac)  [prejudice]",
 "思いこむ": "اِفْتَرَضَ (To authenticate by means of belief; to surmise; to suppose to be true, especiall)  [to assume (that)]\nمثال: 彼が僕にそう思い込ませたのです。\n→ He put the idea into my head. / وَطَّنَ نَفْسَهُ عَلَى, عَزَمَ (To decide; to reach a conclusion.)  [to make up one's mind] / [to be obsessed (with a thought, idea, etc.) ; to think about obsessively]",
 "思いたつ": "وَطَّنَ نَفْسَهُ عَلَى, عَزَمَ (To decide; to reach a conclusion.)  [to make up one's mind]",
 "思いっきし": "[with all one's strength ; with all one's heart] / اِسْتِقَالَة, اِسْتِعْفَاء (The act of resigning.)  [resignation]",
 "思いっきり": "[to one's heart's content ; as much as one wants] / عَزْم, عُزْم (A strong will; the state of being resolute.) / دِقَّة (The degree of fineness with which an image can be recorded or produced, often ex)  [resolution]",
 "思いっ切し": "[with all one's strength ; with all one's heart] / اِسْتِقَالَة, اِسْتِعْفَاء (The act of resigning.)  [resignation]",
 "思いつき": "فِكْرَة, فِكْر (An image of an object that is formed in the mind or recalled by the memory.) / فِكْرَة, فِكْر (More generally, any result of mental activity; a thought, a notion; a way of thi)  [idea]\nمثال: それについて一つ思いつきを言ってもいいですか。\n→ May I make a suggestion about it?",
 "思いつく": "[to think of ; to hit upon]\nمثال: いい考えを思いついた。\n→ A good idea came into my mind. / تَذَكَّرَ (To recall from one's memory; to have an image in one's memory.) / اِسْتَذْكَرَ (To memorize; to put something into memory.)  [to remember]",
 "思いとどまる": "تَنَازَلَ (surrender) / تَخَلَّى (surrender) / اِسْتَسْلَمَ (surrender)  [to give up (an idea or plan)]\nمثال: 私は彼女にスキーを思いとどまらせた。\n→ I argued her out of going skiing.",
 "思いなおす": "غَيَّرَ رَأْيَهُ (To decide differently than one had decided before.)  [to change one's mind]\nمثال: 私はその事柄について彼の父に話すつもりだったが、思い直してやめた。\n→ I was going to speak to his father about that matter, but thought better of it.",
 "思いなす": "اِفْتَرَضَ (To authenticate by means of belief; to surmise; to suppose to be true, especiall)  [to assume]",
 "思いめぐらす": "تَفَكَّرَ, فَكَّرَ (To wonder, think of deeply.)  [to ponder]\nمثال: 彼は自分の将来について思い巡らせていた。\n→ He has been speculating on his future.",
 "思いもかけない": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: 思いもかけずあなたに会えてとてもうれしい。\n→ I'm really happy I ran into you.",
 "思いもよらない": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: あの日彼女に会おうとは思いもよらなかった。\n→ She was the last person I expected to meet that day.",
 "思いも寄らない": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: あの日彼女に会おうとは思いもよらなかった。\n→ She was the last person I expected to meet that day.",
 "思いも掛けない": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: 思いもかけずあなたに会えてとてもうれしい。\n→ I'm really happy I ran into you.",
 "思いやり": "تَعَاطُف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / عَطْف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / حُنُو (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a)  [sympathy]\nمثال: そんな事を言うなんて彼女も思いやりがないね。\n→ It's thoughtless of her to say so.",
 "思いをめぐらす": "تَفَكَّرَ, فَكَّرَ (To wonder, think of deeply.)  [to ponder]\nمثال: 彼は自分の将来に思いをめぐらしていた。\n→ He was meditating on his future life.",
 "思いをめぐらせる": "تَفَكَّرَ, فَكَّرَ (To wonder, think of deeply.)  [to ponder]",
