 "思い出す": "ٱسْتَدْعى (To call back, bring back, or summon (someone) to a specific place, station, etc.) / تَذَكَّرَ (To call back (a situation, event, etc.) to one's mind; to remember; to recollect) / سَحْبٌ (The action or fact of calling someone or something back.)  [to recall]\nمثال: あなたを見るとお兄さんを思い出します。\n→ You remind me of your brother.",
 "思い切り": "[to one's heart's content ; as much as one wants]\nمثال: 私は思いきり働きたい。\n→ I will work to the best of my ability. / عَزْم, عُزْم (A strong will; the state of being resolute.) / دِقَّة (The degree of fineness with which an image can be recorded or produced, often ex)  [resolution]",
 "思い切る": "تَنَازَلَ (surrender) / تَخَلَّى (surrender) / اِسْتَسْلَمَ (surrender)  [to give up (all thoughts of)]\nمثال: 彼女の事が思い切れない。\n→ I can't forget her. / وَطَّنَ نَفْسَهُ عَلَى, عَزَمَ (To decide; to reach a conclusion.)  [to make up one's mind]\nمثال: 重病には思い切った療法が必要だ。\n→ Desperate diseases require desperate remedies.",
