 "思う": "فَكَرَ, فَكَّرَ (To ponder, to go over in one's mind.) / فَكَّرَ (To communicate to oneself in one's mind, to try to find a solution to a problem.) / ظَنَّ (To guess; to reckon; to believe while admittedly being uncertain.)  [to think]\n想う has connotations of heart-felt\nمثال: 晴れだと思うよ。\n→ I think it will be sunny. / فَكَرَ, فَكَّرَ (To ponder, to go over in one's mind.) / فَكَّرَ (To communicate to oneself in one's mind, to try to find a solution to a problem.) / ظَنَّ (To guess; to reckon; to believe while admittedly being uncertain.)  [to think (of doing)] / قَاضٍ, قَاضِيَة (A public official whose duty it is to administer the law, especially by presidin) / حَكَمَ (to sit in judgment on, pass sentence on)  [to judge]\nمثال: 状況は深刻だと思いますか。\n→ Do you regard the situation as serious? / تَخَيَّلَ, تَصَوَّرَ (To form a mental image of something; to envision or create something in one's mi)  [to imagine]\nمثال: 我々が思っているほどには、それほど我々は幸福でもなければ、不幸でもない。\n→ We are never as happy or as unhappy as we imagine.",
