 "悪": "شِرِّير, شَرِير (Intending to harm; malevolent.) / شِرِّير, شَرِير (Morally corrupt.) / شَرّ, سَوْء (Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opp) / شَرّ (Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good)  [evil]\nمثال: いかなる善意の考えもそれ自体はあくでありうる。\n→ Any virtuous idea can be vicious in itself. / شِرِّير (A vile, wicked person.)  [(role of) the villain (in theatre, etc.)]",
 "悪い": "سَيِّئ, وحش (Good, superlative, excellent, cool.)  [bad]\nمثال: 「顔色がわるいけど具合が悪いのかい」「そういうわけでもないよ」\n→ \"You look pale. Are you sick?\" \"Not exactly.\" / فَقِير (With no or few possessions or money, particularly in relation to contemporaries ) / مِسْكِين (Worthy of pity.) / فُقَرَاء (The poor people of a society or the world collectively, the poor class of a soci)  [poor (quality)]\nمثال: 私のステレオはあなたのより音質が悪い。\n→ My stereo set is inferior to yours in sound quality. / شِرِّير, شَرِير (Intending to harm; malevolent.) / شِرِّير, شَرِير (Morally corrupt.) / شَرّ, سَوْء (Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opp) / شَرّ (Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good)  [evil]\nمثال: すいません。あなたに悪いことをしました。\n→ I'm sorry. I did you wrong. / قَبِيح, بَشِع (Displeasing to the eye; aesthetically unpleasing.)  [ugly]\nمثال: 建物は落書きだらけで見た目が悪い。\n→ The graffiti-covered building is ugly to look at.",
