 "悪戯": "مَقْلَب (A practical joke or mischievous trick.)  [prank]\nمثال: 少年たちは時々先生にいたずらしたものだった。\n→ Sometimes the boys would play a trick on their teacher. / شِرِّير, مُؤْذٍ (Troublesome, cheeky, badly behaved, impish, naughty, disobedient; showing a fond)  [mischievous]\nمثال: 私はいたずらな子供を大目に見る事ができない。\n→ I cannot be tolerant of naughty children. / هِوَايَة, هَوَس (An activity that one enjoys doing in one's spare time.)  [hobby] / [playing with (e.g. a lighter) ; fooling around with]\nمثال: 子供に包丁をいたずらさせてはダメだよ。\n→ Don't let your boy play with a knife.",
 "悪戯っ子": "مُشَاغِب (A cheeky person or creature; a troublemaker.)  [rascal]\nمثال: そのいたずらっ娘は何食わぬ顔をした。\n→ The naughty girl assumed an air of innocence. / آلْف (A supernatural being or spirit associated with illness, mischief, and harmful or)  [elf]",
