 "意地尽": "عِنَاد (The state, or an act, of stubbornness or doggedness.)  [obstinacy]",
 "意地尽く": "عِنَاد (The state, or an act, of stubbornness or doggedness.)  [obstinacy]",
 "意地悪": "عَنَى, عَنَى (To convey (a meaning).) / لَئِيم, خَسِيس (Intending to cause harm, successfully or otherwise; bearing ill will towards ano) / مُتَوَسِّط (the statistical value)  [mean]\nمثال: 彼女の意地悪な言葉は結局自分の身に跳ね返ってきた。\n→ Her unkind words boomeranged.",
 "意地悪い": "عَنَى, عَنَى (To convey (a meaning).) / لَئِيم, خَسِيس (Intending to cause harm, successfully or otherwise; bearing ill will towards ano) / مُتَوَسِّط (the statistical value)  [mean]\nمثال: その老人は見かけほど意地悪くなかった。\n→ The old man was not as mean as he looked.",
 "意地汚い": "نَهِم, شَرِه (Given to excessive eating; prone to overeating.) / جَشِع (Greedy.)  [gluttonous]\nمثال: 私の金に意地汚く手を出すな。\n→ Don't put your greedy hands on my money.",
 "意外": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\noft. ～と adverbially\nمثال: 意外な結果が発表された。\n→ Unexpected results were announced.",
 "意字": "رمز تصويري (A picture or symbol which represents the idea of something without indicating th)  [ideogram]",
 "意志": "إرَادَة (One's independent faculty of choice; the ability to be able to exercise one's ch) / رَغْبَة, إرَادَة (The act of choosing to do something; a person’s conscious intent or volition.) / إرَادَة (One's intention or decision; someone's orders or commands.)  [will]\nمثال: 意志に反して何かを無理にさせる事はできない。\n→ No one can force you to do anything against your will.",
 "意志の疎通": "اِتِّصَالَات, اِتِّصَال (The concept or state of exchanging data or information between entities.) / رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A message; the essential data transferred in an act of communication.)  [(reciprocal) communication]",
 "意志の自由": "حُرِّيَّة الْإِرَادَة (The ability to choose one's actions and make choices that are not predetermined )  [free will]",
 "意志疎通": "اِتِّصَالَات, اِتِّصَال (The concept or state of exchanging data or information between entities.) / رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A message; the essential data transferred in an act of communication.)  [(reciprocal) communication]\nمثال: 意思疎通がうまくいかない所では、活動もうまくいかない。\n→ Where communications fail, so do activities.",
 "意思": "قَصْد, إِرَادَة (A course of action that a person intends to follow.)  [intention]\nمثال: 意思伝達は色々な形をとる。\n→ Communication takes many forms.",
 "意思の疎通": "اِتِّصَالَات, اِتِّصَال (The concept or state of exchanging data or information between entities.) / رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A message; the essential data transferred in an act of communication.)  [(reciprocal) communication]",
 "意思疎通": "اِتِّصَالَات, اِتِّصَال (The concept or state of exchanging data or information between entities.) / رِسَالَة, خَبَر (A message; the essential data transferred in an act of communication.)  [(reciprocal) communication]\nمثال: 意思疎通がうまくいかない所では、活動もうまくいかない。\n→ Where communications fail, so do activities.",
 "意想外": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]",
 "意欲": "إرَادَة (One's independent faculty of choice; the ability to be able to exercise one's ch) / رَغْبَة, إرَادَة (The act of choosing to do something; a person’s conscious intent or volition.) / إرَادَة (One's intention or decision; someone's orders or commands.)  [will]\nمثال: その老人は生きる意欲をなくした。\n→ The old man lost the will to live.",
 "意欲的": "مُشْتَاق (Not employing lazy evaluation; calculating results immediately, rather than defe)  [eager]\nمثال: 彼の次の制作は非常に意欲的なミュージカルだった。\n→ His next production was a very ambitious musical.",
 "意気": "رُوح (The soul of a person or other creature.) / رُوَح (A supernatural being, often but not exclusively without physical form; ghost, fa) / كُحُول (A volatile liquid, such as alcohol. The plural form spirits is a generic term fo)  [spirit]\nمثال: 良し、その意気で。\n→ That's the spirit.",
 "意気地": "ثِقَة بِالنَّفْس (The state or degree of being self-confident: believing in one's own abilities.)  [self-confidence]",
 "意気地なし": "جَبَان (A person who lacks courage.)  [coward]",
 "意気地のない": "جَبَان (Lacking in courage or confidence.)  [timid]",
 "意気地無し": "جَبَان (A person who lacks courage.)  [coward]",
 "意気投合": "تَعَاطُف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / عَطْف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / حُنُو (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a)  [sympathy]\nمثال: ボブとはすっかり意気投合した。\n→ I found a kindred spirit in Bob.",
 "意気沮喪": "رَفْض, إِبَاء (The act of rejecting.)  [rejection]",
 "意気消沈": "مُنْخَفَض (An area that is lower in topography than its surroundings.)  [depression]\nمثال: 君の犬は本当に意気消沈しているのだろう。\n→ Your dog may be really depressed.",
 "意気込み": "حَمَاس, حَمَاسَة (An intensity of feeling; an excited interest or eagerness.)  [enthusiasm]\nمثال: おやおや。いかな体育の授業といえど・・・真剣勝負の意気込みで臨まなければ、いざ実戦と言う時に役に立ちませんよ。\n→ Well, even if it is just P.E. class, if you don't take it seriously, it won't do you any good in a real match.",
 "意気阻喪": "رَفْض, إِبَاء (The act of rejecting.)  [rejection]",
 "意義": "مَعْنًى (symbolic value of something) / الْمَعْنَى (symbolic value of something) / مَعْنًى (significance of a thing, as \"the meaning of life\") / مَعْنًى (definition or connotation of a word)  [meaning]\nمثال: レイプ危機運動の内部においては、グリーンサイトによる異議表明は重要な意義を持っている。\n→ Within the rape crisis movement, Greensite's dissent is significant.",
 "意義深い": "هَامّ (Having a noticeable or major effect.)  [significant]\nمثال: 結婚式は、意義深い儀式である。\n→ A wedding is a significant ceremony.",
 "意表": "دَهْشَة, تَعَجُّب (The feeling that something unexpected has happened.) / بَاغَتَ (cause (someone) to feel surprise) / فَاجَأَ (cause (someone) to feel surprise) / دَهِشَ (cause (someone) to feel surprise)  [surprise]",
 "意表外": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]",
 "意見": "رَأْي, نَظَر (A belief, judgment or perspective that a person has formed, either through objec)  [opinion]\nمثال: ここではどんどん意見をおっしゃってかまいません。\n→ You can speak out freely here. / اِمْرَأَة سَلِيطَة (A person who habitually scolds, in particular a troublesome and angry woman.) / وَبَّخَ (To rebuke angrily.)  [scolding]",
 "意見を述べる": "رَأَى, ظَنَّ (To express an opinion; to state as an opinion; to suppose, consider (that).)  [to opine]\nمثال: 私は率直に意見を述べる人を尊敬します。\n→ I admire a person who expresses a frank opinion.",
 "意見交換": "عَصَف ذِهْنِيّ, قَدَح ذِهْنِيّ (A method of problem solving in which members of a group contribute ideas spontan)  [brainstorming]\nمثال: 彼女はガードレールの強度について、ぜひ意見交換をしたいと望んでいます。\n→ She would value the opportunity to exchange views on the strength of guard-rails.",
 "意見書": "جِدَال, مُجَادَلَة (A verbal dispute; a quarrel.) / وَسِيط (A value, or a reference to a value, passed to a function.)  [argument]\nمثال: 彼は意見書を提出した。\n→ He submitted his written opinion.",
 "意識": "وَعْي (awareness) / شُعُور (awareness)  [consciousness]\nمثال: これらのプロセスのどれも意識されていないということを強調することがもっとも重要である。\n→ It is most important to emphasize that none of these processes are conscious. / وعي (The state or level of consciousness where sense data can be confirmed by an obse)  [awareness]\nمثال: このお料理は、パリのエスプリを意識して、味付けしてみました。\n→ This cuisine is seasoned to evoke the esprit of Paris. / [mano-vijnana (mental consciousness, cognizer of sensory information)]",
 "意識が低い": "جَاهِل (Unknowledgeable or uneducated; characterized by ignorance.)  [ignorant]",
 "意識を回復する": "أَنْعَشَ (To restore consciousness, vigor, or life to.)  [to resuscitate]",
 "意識下": "اللَّاوَعِيّ (Occuring in the part of our mind that we are not normally aware of.)  [subconscious]",
 "意識不明": "فِقْدَان اَلْوَعْي, إِغْمَاء (The state of lacking consciousness, of being unconscious)  [(state of) unconsciousness]\nمثال: ときには、機械によって意識不明の人が何年間も呼吸し続けることもあります。\n→ Sometimes machines can make an unconscious person breathe for years.",
