 "愛": "حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [love]\nمثال: 愛の動きは不可解。\n→ Love moves in mysterious ways. / مَوَدَّة (A strong bonding with or fondness for someone or something.) / مُلْحَق (The means by which something is physically attached.) / مُرْفَق (A file sent along with a message, usually an email.)  [attachment] / [agape] / أَيِرْلَنْدَا f or إِيرْلَنْدَا (A large island in northwestern Europe.)  [Ireland]",
 "愛い": "غَرَامَة (A fee levied as punishment for breaking the law.) / غَرَّمَ (To issue a fine as punishment to (someone).)  [fine (person)]\nreferring to someone of lower status",
 "愛おしい": "عَزِيز, عَزِيْزَة (Loved; lovable.) / غَالِي, غَالِيَّة (Precious to or greatly valued by someone.)  [dear]\nمثال: なんでも自分で手がけると、いとおしくなるものです。\n→ Whatever it is, you become fonder of it if you work on it yourself. / فَقِير (With no or few possessions or money, particularly in relation to contemporaries ) / مِسْكِين (Worthy of pity.) / فُقَرَاء (The poor people of a society or the world collectively, the poor class of a soci)  [poor]",
 "愛おしがる": "شَفَقَة (A feeling of sympathy at the misfortune or suffering of someone or something.) / شَفِقَ (To feel pity for (someone or something).)  [to pity]",
 "愛おしむ": "حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [to love]",
 "愛くるしい": "فَاتِن, قَشِيب (Possessing physical features, behaviors, personality traits or other properties )  [cute]\nمثال: 彼女の愛くるしい笑顔を見るとほっとする。\n→ Seeing her lovely face relaxes me.",
 "愛し": "مَحْبُوب (Much loved, dearly loved.) / حَبِيب (Someone who is loved; something that is loved.)  [beloved]",
 "愛しあう": "[to love one another ; to be affectionate towards each other]\nمثال: ジョンとメアリーはお互いに愛し合っていました。\n→ John and Mary loved each other. / ضَاجَعَ, جَامَعَ (To engage in sexual intercourse.)  [to make love]",
 "愛しい": "عَزِيز, عَزِيْزَة (Loved; lovable.) / غَالِي, غَالِيَّة (Precious to or greatly valued by someone.)  [dear]\nمثال: 少女は人形をいとしげに抱き締めた。\n→ The girl squeezed her doll affectionately. / [pitiable ; pitiful]",
