 "感受": "حَاسَّة (Any of the manners by which living beings perceive the physical world: for human) / إِحْسَاس, شُعُور (Perception through the intellect; apprehension; awareness.) / مَعْنَى, دَلَالَة (The meaning, reason, or value of something.) / مَوْهِبَة, قُدْرَة طَبِيعِيَّة (A natural appreciation or ability.) / حَسَّ (To use biological senses: to either see, hear, smell, taste, or feel.)  [sensing] / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, اِسْتَلَمَ (To take, as something that is offered; to accept.) / اِسْتَقْبَلَ, يَسْتَقْبِل (To act as a host for guests; to give admittance to; to permit to enter, as into )  [receiving]",
 "感嘆": "إِعْجَاب (A positive emotion combining wonder and approbation; the regarding of another as)  [admiration]\nمثال: 私たちは富士山の景観に感嘆した。\n→ We admired the view of Mt. Fuji.",
 "感嘆文": "صِيَاح, صُرَاخ (A loud calling or crying out, for example as in surprise, pain, grief, joy, ange)  [exclamation]",
 "感嘆符": "عَلَامَةْ تَعَجُّب, عَلَامَةْ هُتَاف (The punctuation mark “!” (generally used to denote excitement, surprise or shock)  [exclamation mark]\nمثال: 文を書くときには、ふつう大文字で始め、ピリオド（.）、または感嘆符（!）、疑問符（?）、で終わる。\n→ When writing a sentence, generally you start with a capital letter and finish with a period (.), an exclamation mark (!), or a question…",
 "感嘆詞": "حَرْف نِدَاء (An exclamation or filled pause; a word or phrase with no particular grammatical )  [interjection]\nمثال: 「ああ」は感嘆詞だ。\n→ \"Ah\" is an interjection. / صِيَاح, صُرَاخ (A loud calling or crying out, for example as in surprise, pain, grief, joy, ange)  [exclamation]",
 "感度": "اِسْتِقْبَال (The act of receiving.) / اِسْتِقْبَال, حَفْلَة اِسْتِقْبَال (A social engagement, usually to formally welcome someone.)  [reception (radio, TV, etc.)] / [sensitivity (of film)]",
 "感得": "تَحْقِيق (The act of realizing, as:)  [(profound) realization] / [one's faith being transmitted to a deity and one's wish then being granted] / [obtaining (something) unexpectedly]",
 "感心": "إِعْجَاب (A positive emotion combining wonder and approbation; the regarding of another as)  [admiration]\nمثال: 我々は彼女の勇気に感心する。\n→ We admire her for her bravery. / جَدِير بِالْإِعْجَاب (The quality, state, or an example of being admirable.)  [admirable] / ذُهُول, دَهْشَة (The feeling or experience of being astonished; great surprise.)  [astonishment]",
 "感応": "أَجَابَ (To say something in return; to answer; to reply.)  [responding] / [divine response (e.g. to a prayer)] / [divine inspiration] / [induction (electromagnetism) ; inducing]",
 "感応性": "تَعَاطُف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / عَطْف (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a) / حُنُو (feeling of pity or sorrow for the suffering or distress of a)  [sympathy]",
 "感性": "حَاسَّة (Any of the manners by which living beings perceive the physical world: for human) / إِحْسَاس, شُعُور (Perception through the intellect; apprehension; awareness.) / مَعْنَى, دَلَالَة (The meaning, reason, or value of something.) / مَوْهِبَة, قُدْرَة طَبِيعِيَّة (A natural appreciation or ability.) / حَسَّ (To use biological senses: to either see, hear, smell, taste, or feel.)  [sense (of ...)]\nمثال: 少女の鋭い感性に触れている。\n→ I am touched by the girl's acute sensitivity.",
 "感性論": "عِلْم الْجَمَال, فَلْسَفَةُ الْجَمَال (The study or philosophy of beauty.)  [aesthetics]",
 "感恩": "شُكْر, اِمْتِنَان (The state of being grateful.)  [gratitude]",
 "感情": "عَاطِفَة, عَوَاطِف (A person's internal state of being and involuntary physiological response to an )  [emotion]\nمثال: トムは自分の感情をぐっと抑えた。\n→ Tom got a grip on his emotions.",
 "感情移入": "تَعَاطُف (Identification with or understanding of the thoughts, feelings, or emotional sta)  [empathy]",
 "感想": "اِنْطِبَاع, أَثَر (The overall effect of something, e.g., on a person.) / تَقْلِيد (An impersonation, an imitation of the mannerisms of another person.)  [impressions]\nمثال: ゲームについてのご感想は？\n→ How did you feel about the game?",
 "感慨深い": "مُتَحَرِّك (That moves or move.) / مُؤَثِّر (Causing or evoking deep emotions.)  [moving]",
 "感懐": "اِنْطِبَاع, أَثَر (The overall effect of something, e.g., on a person.) / تَقْلِيد (An impersonation, an imitation of the mannerisms of another person.)  [impression]",
 "感服": "إِعْجَاب (A positive emotion combining wonder and approbation; the regarding of another as)  [admiration]\nمثال: 君の勇気には全く感服する。\n→ I admire you for your courage.",
 "感染": "عَدْوَى (The act or process of infecting.) / عَدْوَى (An uncontrolled growth of harmful microorganisms in a host.)  [infection]\nمثال: 「トイレの便座からエイズが感染することってあるの？」「いいえ、ありません」\n→ \"Is it possible to catch AIDS from toilet seats?\" \"No, it isn't.\" / [being infected (e.g. with harmful ideas) ; being influenced (by)]",
 "感染す": "أَعْدَى (To bring (the body or part of it) into contact with a substance that causes illn)  [to infect (someone)]",
 "感染病": "مَرَض مُعْدٍ (An illness caused by a specific infectious agent (bacterium, virus, fungus, prot)  [infectious disease]",
 "感染症": "مَرَض مُعْدٍ (An illness caused by a specific infectious agent (bacterium, virus, fungus, prot)  [infectious disease]\nمثال: 耳の感染症によくかかります。\n→ I often have ear infections.",
 "感染者": "نَاقِل (A person or company in the business of shipping freight.) / مَوْجَة حامِلة (A signal such as radio, sound, or light that is modulated to transmit informatio) / حَامِل, حَمَلَة (A person or other organism that has a genetic trait, mutation or infection liabl)  [carrier (e.g. of a virus)]",
 "感歎符": "عَلَامَةْ تَعَجُّب, عَلَامَةْ هُتَاف (The punctuation mark “!” (generally used to denote excitement, surprise or shock)  [exclamation mark]\nمثال: 文を書くときには、ふつう大文字で始め、ピリオド（.）、または感嘆符（!）、疑問符（?）、で終わる。\n→ When writing a sentence, generally you start with a capital letter and finish with a period (.), an exclamation mark (!), or a question…",
 "感歎詞": "حَرْف نِدَاء (An exclamation or filled pause; a word or phrase with no particular grammatical )  [interjection]\nمثال: 「ああ」は感嘆詞だ。\n→ \"Ah\" is an interjection. / صِيَاح, صُرَاخ (A loud calling or crying out, for example as in surprise, pain, grief, joy, ange)  [exclamation]",
 "感涙": "مَزَّقَ, شَقَّ (To rend (a solid material) by holding or restraining in two places and pulling a) / خَرْق, شَقّ (A hole or break caused by tearing.) / دَمْع, دَمْعَة (A drop of clear, salty liquid produced from the eyes by crying or irritation.) / دَمَعَ (To produce tears.)  [tears (from being deeply moved)]",
 "感潮域": "مَصَبّ, فُغْرَة (A coastal water body where ocean tides and river water merge, resulting in a bra)  [estuary]",
 "感激": "اِنْطِبَاع, أَثَر (The overall effect of something, e.g., on a person.) / تَقْلِيد (An impersonation, an imitation of the mannerisms of another person.)  [impression]\nمثال: 彼の言葉で彼女は感激のあまり涙ぐんだ。\n→ His words moved her to tears.",
 "感知": "اِدْرََاك حَسِّيّ (Conscious understanding of something.)  [perception]\nمثال: 説得不能を感知してか、黒崎先生はため息をついて席に着いた。\n→ Perhaps having realized it was impossible to persuade her, Ms. Kurosaki sighed and sat down in her seat.",
 "感知器": "حَسَّاس, جِهَازُ اِسْتِشْعَار (A device or organ that detects certain external stimuli and responds in a distin)  [sensor]",
 "感興": "فَائِدَة (The price paid for obtaining, or price received for providing, money or goods in)  [interest]",
 "感覚": "حَاسَّة (Any of the manners by which living beings perceive the physical world: for human) / إِحْسَاس, شُعُور (Perception through the intellect; apprehension; awareness.) / مَعْنَى, دَلَالَة (The meaning, reason, or value of something.) / مَوْهِبَة, قُدْرَة طَبِيعِيَّة (A natural appreciation or ability.) / حَسَّ (To use biological senses: to either see, hear, smell, taste, or feel.)  [sense]\nمثال: 私は指に感覚が無かった。\n→ I had no feeling in my fingers.",
 "感覚的": "بَدِيهِيٌّ (Spontaneous, without requiring conscious thought.)  [intuitive]\nمثال: 感覚的にそれに違和感を感じるが、一体それが何なのかわからなかった。\n→ Even though I felt that there was something strange, I just didn't know what it was.",
 "感触": "تحسس (To use or experience the sense of touch.) / شَعَرَ (To sense or think emotionally or judgmentally.) / شَعَرَ بِ (To sense or think emotionally or judgmentally.)  [feel (of something)]\nمثال: これはシルクの感触だ。\n→ This feels like silk. / شُعُور, إِحْسَاس (Sensation, particularly through the skin.) / عَاطِفَة, إِحْسَاس (Emotion; impression.)  [feeling]",
 "感謝": "شُكْرًا (Used to express appreciation or gratitude.)  [thanks]\nمثال: ご協力に感謝します。\n→ I appreciate your cooperation.",
 "感謝祭": "عِيد اَلشُّكْر (Thanksgiving Day)  [Thanksgiving (Day)]\nمثال: 感謝祭のお休み、楽しんでね。\n→ Have a nice Thanksgiving! / [customer appreciation event ; thank you (for your patronage) sales campaign]",
 "慄き": "اِرْتَجَفَ, اِقْشَعَّرَ (To tremble or shake, especially when cold or frightened.)  [shiver]",
 "慄く": "هَزَّ (To cause (something) to move rapidly in opposite directions alternatingly.) / هَزَّ (To move from side to side.)  [to shake (from fear, cold, excitement, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼女は声をおののかせて「助けて！」と叫んだ。\n→ In a quivering voice she cried \"Help!\"",
 "慇懃": "أَدِيب, مُؤَدَّب (Well-mannered, civilized.)  [polite]\nمثال: 彼のいんぎんさは本心ではないかもしれない。\n→ His cordiality may not be authentic. / صَدَاقَة (The condition of being friends.) / صَدَاقَة (A friendly relationship, or a relationship as friends.)  [friendship]",
 "慈しみ": "حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [love]",
 "慈しむ": "حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [to love]\nمثال: 死がまさに我らを引離すまで愛し、いつくしむ。\n→ To love and to cherish, till death do us part.",
 "慈善": "مُنَظَّمَة خَيْرِيَّة (An organization, the objective of which is to carry out a charitable purpose.) / صَدَقَة (The goods or money given to those in need, or the act of doing it.) / إِحْسَان (Benevolence to the less fortunate; the providing of goods or money to those in n)  [charity]\nمثال: その隠れた慈善を彼がしたことだと世間では信じている。\n→ They accredit him with the secret charity.",
 "慈善団体": "جَمْعِيَّة خَيْرِيَّة (An organization with charitable purposes only.)  [charitable organization]\nمثال: ある気前の良い男性が、およそ二十億円を慈善団体に寄付した。\n→ A generous man contributed some two billion yen to charity.",
 "慈善家": "سَخِيّ (A person or institution who seeks to improve the world, especially by monetary g)  [philanthropist]",
 "慈善心": "النزعَة إلى الخير (Disposition to do good.)  [benevolence]",
 "慈心": "النزعَة إلى الخير (Disposition to do good.)  [benevolence]",
 "慈悲": "رَحْمَة, رَأْفَة (Relenting; forbearance to cause or allow harm to another.) / رَحْمَة, شَفَقَة (Forgiveness or compassion, especially toward those less fortunate.)  [mercy]\nمثال: ヤッパリさんが裁判官に慈悲を求めて訴えた。\n→ Mr. Yappari appealed to the judge for mercy. / [rufous hawk-cuckoo ; northern hawk-cuckoo]",
 "慈悲心": "رَحْمَة (deep awareness of the suffering of another) / شَفَقَة (deep awareness of the suffering of another)  [compassion]",
 "慈悲深い": "شَفَقَة (Having, feeling or showing compassion (to or toward someone).)  [compassionate]",
 "慈愛": "حَبِيب, حَبِيبَة (A person who is the object of romantic feelings; a darling, a sweetheart, a belo) / أَحَبَّ, حب (To have a strong affection for (someone or something).) / أَحَبَّ (To be strongly inclined towards something; an emphatic form of like.)  [love]\nمثال: 慈愛は家庭から始まる。\n→ Charity begins at home.",
 "慈鳥": "غُرَاب, زَاغ (A bird, usually black, of the genus Corvus, having a strong conical beak, with p) / صَاحَ (To make the shrill sound characteristic of a rooster; to make a sound in this ma)  [crow]",
 "態": "ظُهُور (The act of appearing or coming into sight; the act of becoming visible to the ey) / مَظْهَر (A thing seen; a phenomenon; an apparition.) / مَظْهَر, شَكْل (The way something looks; personal presence) / شَكْل (Apparent likeness; the way which something or someone appears to others.)  [appearance]\nمثال: 奥さんのがみがみ小言にフレッドさんは大弱りの体であった。\n→ Fred was very troubled by his wife's nagging.",
 "態勢": "مَوْقِف, سُلُوك (A disposition or state of mind.)  [attitude]\nمثال: ５００人の警官が厳重な警備態勢おかれた。\n→ 500 policemen were put on strict alert."
}
